PATCH 498: the 9e2b state-table handlers 9f1d / a07c and their shared helpers a135 / a15a.

Patch 497 repaired the `call *%cs:0x9f0f(%bx)` table base in FUN_0000_9e2b, which made this family
reachable for the first time; INDIA1 and TRAIN3 then SIGSEGV'd on the first frame the state machine ran,
both at 9f1d <- 9e2b <- c0e5 <- c0ca <- 459a.

9e2b dispatches with DI = the object's DGROUP NEAR OFFSET, so it arrives in param_1 (the fault backtrace
shows param_1 = 0xbbd9, a live roster offset, while Ghidra's chosen param_3 = 0xffffcc28).  All four
functions carry the same three defects:

  * the object -- and the SECOND near offset word[di+0x1f], the tracked target -- were dereferenced as
    host pointers;
  * the WORD comparands/stores [di+0x21] / [di+0x23] / [di+0x2e] were read and written as 4-byte ints
    (the [di+0x2e] store clobbers [di+0x30], the desired heading);
  * a135/a15a dropped FUN_0000_054c's CX and DX outputs.  054c (asm 0x54c-0x577) pushes 08e8's AX/DX
    before calling 077e and pops them back, so on return AX=bearing, BX=pitch, CX=range_lo, DX=range_hi,
    with CX/DX being exactly DGROUP:0x458/0x45a (DAT_1000_c458/c45a).  The asm then composes
    `mov ch,cl ; mov dl,ch` = ((range_hi & 0xff) << 8) | ((range_lo >> 8) & 0xff) == (uint16_t)(range>>8)
    -- the same idiom patch 328 restored in ab91 -- and stores it at [di+0x21].  Ghidra's __allregs model
    returns AX only, so it folded that store onto a135/a15a's own DEAD INPUTS param_1/param_2.

a135's two remaining call sites are FUN_0000_9f1d and FUN_0000_a07c (both fixed here) and
FUN_0000_9f0f.  The last is not a function: 0x9f0f IS the dispatch table (verified contents
{9f1d, 9f66, 9fe5, a069, a07c, a02a}), which Ghidra typed as code -- its body decodes to `in(0x9f)` and
a chain of writes through a fabricated `puVar1`, it has no caller and no entry in the icall map, so it
is left untouched rather than "corrected"; a135's signature is preserved so it still compiles.
